{
  "$comment": "Projections (ADR 0148; docs/migration-design.md, 'Stages 5 and 6'): what a spelling says, read forwards off its letters by the profile's stated correspondences (sound-read), two spellings compared by sound (sound-compare: same, free, and the places they differ), a word's other spellings of its sound (sound-spellings); and a reading scheme's relation to the spelling it annotates (reading-spells, by dynamic programming), the pieces a script leaves open (reading-variants) and minimal ruby (reading-open). Profiles: es-Latn/standard (Cuban: seseo, yeísmo, b/v, silent h, stress), fa-Arab/standard (ADR 0142's sets); schemes: schluessel (of chg-Arab/standard), pinyin and baxter (sets only).",
